## Control {{controlId}}: Store and Transmit Only Cryptographically-Protected Passwords

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization stores and transmits only cryptographically-protected passwords within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Entra ID password hashing, TLS-encrypted transmission, and CUI group access controls managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
**CUI Account Management:**
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) defines the population of accounts authorized for CUI access. All accounts within this group use cryptographically protected credentials:
- Passwords are hashed using industry-standard algorithms (bcrypt/PBKDF2) before storage in Entra ID
- Password transmission occurs exclusively over TLS-encrypted channels (TLS 1.2+)
- No plaintext passwords are stored in any M365 service, configuration file, or log
{{else}}
CUI access group has not been configured. Cryptographic password protection applies to all tenant accounts through Entra ID defaults.
{{/if}}

{{#if userCount}}
**User Account Coverage:**
{{userCount}} user accounts in the tenant directory use cryptographically protected credentials. Self-service password reset (SSPR) uses encrypted channels for password change operations.
{{/if}}

{{#if mfaEnabled}}
**Additional Credential Protection:**
MFA reduces reliance on passwords alone. {{authMethodsCount}} authentication methods provide cryptographic credential verification beyond password-based authentication.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Entra ID password hash configuration, TLS enforcement settings, SSPR configuration, and credential storage audit logs.

